# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text Seven ships stand on the flat in the settling brown, three kilometres short of a glow. At midnight the board cleared one more command, lights only, and {A} sent it, the next ship reading it back. At two kilometres up the brown turned white from underneath: Cargo 2, spending the battery it had saved on every floodlight it owned. Seven pilots, each blind in their own plume, checked their radar against the same glow. {B} set down closest. By dawn the glow is one lamp; by noon it is out, and it stays out. The first crate out of the hold says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. The eighth kept the lights on."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text {B}'s ship is the one the gust caught. It stands upright on the slope three kilometres from Cargo 2, a leg strut folded under it, and the first walk-round says what the readouts said: it will not fly home. {B} sits on the bottom rung for a long minute, then starts a list of what it can still be: habitat, store, radio mast. Two sols later {A}, who wanted to answer from the start, climbs the rim with a second suit at the foot of it, counts the dark between flares, and answers from two hundred metres, inside the tick. HELLO RX · OK. To Starbase: "Landed. Seven down, six to fly. Found the eighth."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three in the long orbit, night pass, half rations on seven galley tables. Below, the storm; on the night side, one lamp, steady since the handshake, blinking twice as the fleet passes over. Cargo 2 sends its manifest a line a pass. Tonight {A} reads: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Seven hungry people cheer a drill bit. Next pass: seed stock, frozen in week two, the night the lamp stayed lit and the hold heater didn't. {B}, who argued to wait, logs it. A week later the storm clears, and the lamp blinks them down. The first crate says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Dawn on the rim, frost on the wing. The long orbit is over: by last night all seven ships were down on the flat. For two weeks a battery under that frost has been choosing which knock to skip, and the strobe has been dark since midnight. {A} kneels at the service port with a battery pack and a radio, {B} a step behind in the second suit, counting aloud. Clip, latch, wait. Nine. Ten. Eleven. A click, slow, like something clearing its throat. The answer goes in by hand, from two metres, inside the tick. HELLO RX · OK. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Old Friend
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol, thirty kilometres out, {A} driving, {B} on the battery: past half, and Cargo 2's knock on the rover radio no louder. There and back is more than the rover has. {A} keeps driving. Two kilometres out, Cargo 2 hears the rover and runs the pad crew's routine for a truck from the hangar: floods, hatch lamp, and the charge port on its landing leg, warm, its battery full since the strobe went off. {B} plugs in at four percent. The pack never takes a full charge again; the only rover runs at half range from now on. The first crate says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol, two hundred metres from Cargo 2, nose to the strobe, {A} and {B} in the cab. On the first sol Cargo 3's drill snapped its only bit; the spare is in that hold. The rover's spare batteries went into its heaters on the second night; the last one is flat. {A} counts the dark: nine, ten, eleven, flare, and answers. HELLO RX · OK. The hold unlatches. Then Cargo 2 does what the pad patch says, wakes every survival heater at once with no battery check, and the strobe goes out for good. They drive back on the rover's main pack, heaters off, the bit in {B}'s lap. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth, in time."

